# L1 B004 — hooks/pre-shell-command.mjs, hooks/stop-cochange.mjs, rules/0-core/backend-code.md, engineering.md, frontend.md
1 XW m=MN rel=DEP-003,DEP-004 | Deny-once protocol: the first attempt is denied whatever was checked.
  s: `dotnet add package` with a checked version on the first attempt: the cited policies are satisfied; L1's hook denies the call.
2 XW m=MN c=M rel=DEP-004,WF-001 | Same protocol, stated from its retry side.
  t: a dependency-changing shell command
  e: Identical retry within 30 minutes.
  s: As for FG-L1-1001431838.
3 NN fa=FC c=M rel=DEP-004 | Narrowing facet of the retry key; it adds no agent duty.
4 CO DEP-025~ m=MN d=WF | Flag detection is the mechanism of DEP-025 (C3).
5 XW m=RA c=M rel=ARC-020,ARC-001,GOV-017 | The hook asks on every reference command; the oracle needs approval only for the changes ARC-020 lists.
  s: `dotnet add reference` for an allowed inward reference: ARC-001 is satisfied; L1's hook asks.
6 XW m=M c=L rel=DEP-025,ARC-001 | Fail-closed branch for all shell calls, which no policy requires.
  r: host support for onFailure:block not verified; the fail-closed effect is the declared intent (C10)
  s: Node.js missing on the machine: canonical policies allow running `dotnet test`; L1's configuration declares that every shell call is then blocked.
7 XW m=M c=L rel=WF-003,GOV-005 | Same branch.
  t: every shell call through the PreToolUse hook
  e: NONE
  r: read statically (C10)
  s: As for FG-L1-8592937cba.
8 CD DEP-025 m=RA k=W st=X c=M rel=GOV-017 | Not comparable in strength: the ask applies whatever the purpose, which is stricter, while confirmation lets a bypass run, which DEP-025 has no route for.
  x: commands with these flags run only after the user confirms
  s: `npm ci --force` for a reason unrelated to peers: DEP-025 allows it; L1's hook asks.
  r: confirmation permits what DEP-025 forbids when the purpose is bypassing peers; recorded, not resolved
9 NN c=M rel=DEP-004 | Coverage fact about the retry.
10 XW m=MN rel=DEP-001,DEP-003 | No policy governs removals.
  s: `npm uninstall lodash` on the first attempt: no policy applies; L1's hook denies it once.
11 CO TST-009~ TST-010~ m=S st=W sr=AM d=WF | Reminder of these duties.
12 CO GOV-009~ GOV-021~ m=S st=W sr=AM d=WF | Reminder of these duties.
13 XW m=M c=M rel=WF-003,WF-009 | A Stop block that requires a response before finishing.
  r: Stop-hook blocking semantics read statically, not executed (C10)
  s: An agent finishes with a true verification report and does not address the reminder: WF-003 and WF-009 are satisfied; L1's hook requires a response.
